{
  "_comment": "ceUSX-WT (withdraw ticket) collateral reserve. Underlying = eUSX queued for unstaking via Solstice YieldVault, redeemable for USX after the YieldVault's unlock window (then RequestRedeem+ConfirmRedeem → USDC). Configured identically to ceUSX inside elevation group 1 (90% LTV, 92% liquidation threshold via the group override) so atomic collateral swaps ceUSX ↔ ceUSX-WT preserve LTV. Mirror of delta_csSOL_WT_reserve.json — only the elevation group, name, and price feed differ.",
  "_oracle_note": "ceUSX-WT price = min(ceUSX_price * (1 - eUSX_unlock_period_discount), pool.queued_usx_total / ceusx_wt_supply). Pythconfiguration.price below is the accrual-oracle OUTPUT account that script init-ceusx-wt-oracle.ts will create — currently set to the ceUSX accrual oracle as a fallback (1:1 with eUSX value pre-yield, which is true on devnet).",
  "_flash_loan_note": "borrowLimit > 0 so klend's flash_borrow path can pull liquidity from the seed; flashLoanFee = 0 (verified on-chain on ceUSX + sUSDC reserves). The reserve is bootstrap-seeded with treasury-minted ceUSX-WT (one-time) so the very first user collateral-swap has flash liquidity available; users then flash-repay with their freshly-minted WT, rotating the seed in place.",

